<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Berat</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Berat is a city in south-central Albania on the Osum river, dominated by a hilltop citadel. Contested in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgarians">Bulgarians</a>, Angevins and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a>, it withstood an Angevin siege in 1281. It was held by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muzaka-family">Muzaka family</a> before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> took it in 1417, and its Ottoman-era quarters of white houses form a World Heritage Site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/berat.jpg" alt="Berat" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Arianit · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Berat_57.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
